בּוֺא 1i , מָבוֺא 2 ); as giving daylight Isa 60:9 ; hot 1Sam 11:9 ; Neh 7:3 ; Exod 16:21 (P), compare Isa 49:10 ; Jonah 4:8 ; Psa 121:6 ; as ripening crops Deut 33:14 (poem), compare (figurative) Job 8:16 , tanning the face Song 1:6 ; standing still at Joshua's word Josh 10:12 .13 a (poem in J; || יָרֵחַ ), 10:13 b (J), compare Hab 3:11 (+ יָרֵךְַ ); casting shadow (on dial), בַּשּׁ אָחָז בְמַעֲלוֺת ׳יָָֽרְדָה Isa 38:8 , הַשּׁ ׳וַתָּשָׁב 38:8 ; set in sky by ׳י Jer 31:25 ; Psa 19:5 ; 74:16 ; 136:8 , enduring 72:5 ; 72:17 (compare עִם 1g ; [ מָּנֶה ] 11. 4 a ( e ), p. 817), also Psa 89:37 ; personified, called to praise ׳י 148:3 (+ יָרֵךְַ ); to be darkened by ׳י s judgment, Ezek 32:7 ; Joel 2:10 ; 3:4 ; Joel 4:15 (compare Amos 8:9 above, Micah 3:6 ). 2 of direction: הַשּׁ ׳מִמִּוְרַח Num 21:11 (E) toward sun-rise, = East , compare Deut 4:41 , 47 16 t. (see מִוְרָךְ p. 280); הַשּׁ ׳מְבוֺא 11:30 3 t. (see מָבוֺא 2 , p. 99). 3 object of worship (usually + moon, stars, etc.) 2Kin 23:5 ; Jer 8:2 ; Ezek 8:16 ; Deut 4:19 ; horses given to ׳שׁ 2Kin 23:11 , השּׁ ׳מַרְכְּבוֺת 23:11 . &#8212; See also שׁ ׳בֵּית p. 112:b. 4 other phrase: a. חַשּׁ ׳נֶגֶד , i.e. openly, publicly , 2Sam 12:12 ; Num 25:4 (P), so חַשּׁ ׳לְעֵינֵי 2Sam 12:11 . b. figurative of living , שׁ ׳חָזָה Psa 58:9 , שׁ ׳רָאָה Exod 6:5 ; 7:11 ; 11:7 , opposed to הַשׁ ׳תֶּחְשַׁךְ 12:2 . c. הַשּׁ ׳תַּחַת , i. e. on the earth, Eccl 1:3 28t. Ecclesiastes (compare Greek ὐφ’ ἠλίῳ , Kue Ond. iii. 196 ; Ein1. iii. 192). 5 pinnacle , as glittering, shining , plural Isa 54:12 thy pinnacles, battlements (of Zion), so perhaps singular ׳שׁ י ׳וּמָנֵן אֱםהִים Psa 84:12 battlement and shield is ׳י ׳א (Gr Bae Du Buhl; most sun , and so Thes De Che SS; Hup-Now hesitates). I. שׁמשׁ (√ of following; Biblical Hebrew שֶׁ֫מֶשׁ שׁמשׁ, ).","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to be brilliant ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 22 36","keyReferences":["1Kgs 22 36","1Sam 11 9"